notes/tech/design-patterns/singleton.content:
Singleton
non-pythonic
class Database:
    __db = None
    def __init__(self):
        self.connection = &quot;connection&quot;
    @classmethod
    def create_connection(cls):
        if cls.__db:
           return cls.__db
        else:
           cls.__db = Database()
           return cls.__db
Some pythonic ways
class Database(object):
    __instance = None
    def __new__(cls, *args, **kwargs):
        if cls.__instance is None:
            cls.__instance = super().__new__(cls, *args, **kwargs)
        return cls.__instance


db1 = Database()

db2 = Database()

db1 is db2 # true
Singleton method in python is always avoided. It becomes hard to test singleton classes as everytime we need to reset the singleton object to its initial state.
Reference

python-patterns.guide/gang-of-four/singleton/

